## Previously raised findings (review-round registry)

These defects were raised on earlier review rounds of this PR. For each finding below: verify fixed (cite the fixing hunk), withdraw (reason required), or mark re-introduced. New claims need new evidence — a claim already on this list is answered, not re-raised.

| id | status | severity | file | claim |
|----|--------|----------|------|-------|
| F1 | open | IMPORTANT | flutter_app/lib/ui/screens/app_launcher_screen.dart | ⚠️ important the responsive 4 6 8 grid contract is now evaluated against a double reduced width builddraggablegrid pre subtracts the scroll view s gutters before calling crossaxiscount app launcher screen dart 1498 maxwidth duorailinset 32 but crossaxiscount subtracts the same 32pt again at line 1620 — the fit reserves 64pt for a 32pt gutter pair so a full launcher can drop one track whenever the pane sits within 32pt above a column boundary the same reduced width is then fed to fawindowclassforwidth width line 1629 which changes the embedded non fullscreen 4 6 8 contract not just the fit the codebase resolves the window class from the window width everywhere else messenger app panel dart 93 wide layout shell dart 891 use mediaquery sizeof context width breakpoints are 640 1024 in fa ui lib src theme fa2 tokens dart a 700pt wide fold pane that used to classify medium → 6 configured columns now classifies small → 4 columns 700 − 32 668 ≥ 640 is medium but 668 − 32 636 640 is small — the grid visibly jumps from six to four wider cells across a 32pt band suggested fix pass the real pane width for the fawindowclassforwidth contract and use the lane width rail 32 once only for fittedtracks dart int crossaxiscount double width final lanewidth math max 0 0 width 32 remove the inner 32 final crossaxiscount crossaxiscount constraints maxwidth let the method do the gutter math once secondary same method fittedtracks clamp 1 24 hardcodes 24 where the store contract caps at launcherlayoutstore maxgridcolumns 8 — fine if the full screen bypass is intentional but a named constant would keep the store bounds discoverable |
| F2 | open | SUGGESTION | flutter_app/lib/network/device_display.dart | 💡 suggestion this new fallback contradicts the function s own documented contract the doc comment two lines up unchanged context device display dart 21 22 still states first prompt snippets stay previews they never stand in for the session name but the new base chain does exactly that for the clifallback path with no registry title and no path a session row s title becomes cli · first prompt snippet devicesessionpreviewtitle preview before the shortdeviceid fallback callers in devices page dart agentsessioncard remotesessioncard pass preview metadata snippet with clifallback true so remote rows without metadata titles now render snippet derived titles the behavior itself looks intentional and stable snippet is the first prompt fallback per presence engine dart 193 194 so the title doesn t churn with each message — but the contract sentence above it is now false and the next reader will fix one of the two please update the doc to state the real chain registry title → project basename → first prompt snippet cli fallback only → first8…last4 or keep snippets preview only and drop them from the title chain |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

